  "tagline": "Multi-model database for IoT and observability: time series, full-text, vector and key-value on Parquet.",
  "description": "Datalayers is a commercial distributed database from China aimed at observability, IoT and AI retrieval. It combines time-series storage, BM25 full-text search, vector search (IVF and HNSW), a Redis-compatible key-value model and SQL stream processing behind one SQL interface, with storage and compute separated over object storage in Parquet format. Clients connect over the PostgreSQL wire protocol or Arrow Flight SQL, and it accepts InfluxDB line protocol and Prometheus remote write, so existing collectors plug in. It is designed to run on edge gateways as well as in cloud clusters. Releases are frequent, but documentation is mostly in Chinese and the product is licence-key based rather than open source.",
